1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial video, we use the 11th version of Doshi Marvelous Designer.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
If you need to learn the 10th version of Marvelous Designer, please watch the previous video.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
In order to make it easier to learn, the Doshi Marvelous Designer is used in this tutorial.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Now let's learn how to create a template in 2D window.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
First of all, we need to import a virtual model.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
In this tutorial video, we will use Feifei from FemaleVR.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Stop your mouse on the multidirectional tool, and select the rectangle tool after clicking on the drop-down menu.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Start from the center of the model, hold down the left mouse button and drag the mouse.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Draw a rectangle according to the body shape of the virtual model, and send the mouse to the appropriate position.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Change the texture display type to semi-transparent surface.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Now you can adjust the template by using the virtual model screenshot.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now you can adjust the template by using the virtual model screenshot.

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Now you can adjust the template by using the virtual model screenshot.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
When the mouse is stuck on the tool, click on Add Marker on the lower left.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In the line in front, at the lowest position of the ruler and the highest position of the line,

16
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Press the left mouse button separately to add 2 points.

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Then add 1 point at the bottom of the page.

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Just make sure that there are some points below the bottom of the model screenshot,

19
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,000
rather than the one below the model screenshot.

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Then select the tool of editing HTML,

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
When we have confirmed these points, we can delete the excess points.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
And this point on the outside of the shoulder, we adjust it according to the angle of the shoulder line.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Please note that this shoulder line is as parallel to the model's shoulder as possible,

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
which helps to create a more harmonious clothing pattern.

25
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Next, let's draw the collar and sleeve curve lines.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
In the drop-down menu, find the editor curve point tool,

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
click on the straight line to create a curve point.

28
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Drag the curve point to adjust the corner of the collar and other panels as a straight line,

29
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
so that it will become a smooth curve when pasting other panels.

30
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Use the same method to draw the sleeve curve,

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
and also maintain the corner of the collar as a straight line.

32
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
You can increase the curve point to adjust the details.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The sleeve curve line is shaped into a straight line,

34
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
and the upper curve is more flat, and the bottom curve is obvious.

35
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Now we have completed one side of the front panel.

36
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Please select the adjustment panel tool.

37
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
On this panel, click on the mouse button on the right and select copy.

38
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
On the right,

39
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
click on the empty place in the background and select mirror pasting.

40
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Next, we will modify this mirror pasting panel to the back panel.

41
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
In the previous tutorial of the 3D window of the creation panel,

42
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
we have mentioned that the collar of the back panel is a little lighter than the front panel.

43
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
First, use the editor curve tool to increase the center point of the back neck,

44
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
and then use the editor curve point tool to adjust the shape of the back collar.

45
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Due to the back curve of the person,

46
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
the curve of the back curve is more flat,

47
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
and it is not like the front panel to consider the impact of the chest.

48
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,000
The sleeve curve of the back panel is more flat compared to the front panel,

49
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
and the curve of the curve of the bottom curve is shorter,

50
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
and the curve is also larger.

51
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
In the tool group of the editor panel,

52
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
find the editor curve tool in the menu,

53
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
click and drag the curve to follow the video to complete the adjustment.

54
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
You can also use the editor curve point tool to complete the adjustment.

55
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Next, let's learn how to create a sleeve panel.

56
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Let's learn how to create a sleeve panel.

57
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Select the rectangle tool and draw a half-sleeved sleeve panel.

58
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Draw a rectangle that is wider than the arm,

59
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
the length can be customized,

60
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
then use the adjustment panel tool to rotate it to the parallel position of the arm,

61
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
and align the highest point to the sharp point.

62
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Select the plus point line tool,

63
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
add a point near the bottom of the page.

64
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
After completion, switch to the adjustment panel tool,

65
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
right-click on the panel,

66
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
select Rotate X-axis,

67
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
then click on the bottom to rotate the panel back.

68
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Now we can delete the excess points.

69
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Now we will use the editor curve tool to adjust the sleeve panel line.

70
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Please add curve points and adjust according to the effect in the video.

71
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
The front sleeve panel line is usually from top to bottom,

72
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
first protruding and then arching,

73
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
the point is in the middle position.

74
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Now we are going to adjust the curve,

75
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
we have completed half of the sleeve panel,

76
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
use the edit panel tool,

77
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
right-click on the middle line,

78
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
select Open,

79
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
the panel will open along this line.

80
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Please note that because the sleeve itself is not a symmetrical shape,

81
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
so here we choose to open,

82
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
instead of opening the editor in a symmetrical way.

83
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Think about our previous panels,

84
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
compared to the front panel,

85
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
the back panel will be wider,

86
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
and the curve point will be a little lower.

87
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
So we need to choose the edit panel tool,

88
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
adjust the sleeve panel line.

89
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
When modifying the sleeve panel line,

90
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
we can move the front panel's curve points inwards a little bit,

91
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
to narrow down the width of the sleeve on this side.

92
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
On the contrary,

93
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
for the back panel,

94
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
we need to move the curve point of the protruding curve line outwards,

95
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
to widen the width of the sleeve on this side.

96
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
And the curve point from the protruding curve line to the arching curve line,

97
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
is about one-third to one-fourth of the sleeve panel,

98
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
and the back panel is about one-third to one-fourth of the sleeve panel.

99
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Now a sleeve panel is completed.

100
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
After we finish the curve line,

101
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
we can adjust more details.

102
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Choose the edit panel tool,

103
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
right-click on each panel,

104
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
and select the column symmetrical panel,

105
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
panel and curve line,

106
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
and then click OK.

107
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
When a panel is in a symmetrical relationship,

108
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
modify one of the panels,

109
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
and the other panel will also be symmetrical.

110
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
When moving the symmetrical panel from the curve,

111
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,000
press the Shift key to place the panel in the horizontal direction.

112
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Do the same for the back panel and the sleeve panel.

113
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Next, let's make the chest pocket.

114
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Select the mouse on the multidirectional tool,

115
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
and then select the rectangle tool in the drop-down menu.

116
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
In the 3D window,

117
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
click on the appropriate position,

118
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:29,000
and then you can use the blue reference point that appears at the same time in the 2D window,

119
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
to draw the pocket line.

120
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
The two front panels will also appear in the internal rectangle,

121
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
because there is a symmetrical relationship between these two panels.

122
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
These internal rectangles are the seam positions of the pockets.

123
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Next, we are going to remove the pocket panel,

124
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
and select the mouse on the edit panel tool,

125
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
and then select the pocket line in the drop-down menu.

126
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
In the frame selection,

127
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
the internal rectangle is right-clicked on the selected position,

128
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
and then select the pocket panel.

129
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Please note that the pocket panel is not symmetrical,

130
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
but an independent panel.

131
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Now that we have completed the creation of the T-shirt panel,

132
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
please save this project as a project file.

133
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
In the follow-up tutorial,

134
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,000
we will learn how to arrange and separate these panels

135
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
to complete the complete costume.

136
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
In the next video,

137
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
we will learn how to do it.

138
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
In this video,

139
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
we will learn how to do it.

